WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.300
Sheets stack up. The figure 9,600 appears, then the stack resolves to one research note with a particle diagram.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:20.700
The printed figure becomes an animation. Its clustered dots move apart.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:29.467
An underline traces the claim to its source. Three drawings show the cloud at successive stages.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:41.800
A line of TypeScript is typed. A React component branches into particles and a label. SVG draws them, then the dots move as the frame number advances.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:56.900
A single waveform draws across the screen. A phrase locks to its timing mark. The dots spread when the narrator says “spread.”

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:07.333
Three frames appear side by side, slide together and acquire an audio track. They resolve into one MP4 file.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:20.600
The file shows its frame count, 4K dimensions and audio check. A rendered frame is compared with the paper, then the animation plays.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:28.800
The cloud spreads before its label appears. A movement reverses. A timing marker slides back to the voice cue, and the corrected spread and label play together.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.000
Imagine Science and github.com/iamnikhiliyer/imagine-science appear.
